      "en": "Fitch Ratings raised its outlook for Portugal's economy to positive from negative, citing the bailed-out euro-zone nation's strong economic recovery and falling budget deficit. Fitch evaluates a country's ability to pay its debts then issues a rating but also issues outlooks on those countries' economies. Fitch affirmed the country's BB+ rating and said its fiscal financing conditions have improved substantially since October 2013, the date of its last Portugal ratings review. A BB+ rating corresponds to a speculative investment and a skeptical view of a country paying back its debts. The ratings agency raised its economic forecasts for Portugal and now sees gross domestic product (GDP) growth of 1.3% this year and 1.5% in 2015, sharply up from 0.2% and 1% previously. Fitch noted that the economy grew on an annual basis for the first time in three years in the last quarter of 2013, by 1.6%. *(online.wsj.com)*",
